nical specification (all ten protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-73435","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104732","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-008-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-104733","text":" — the Agent Harness Protocol specification"}]}],"id":"blk-73437","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104734","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-104735","text":" — PRISM diagnostic benchmark protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-73439","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104736","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-104737","text":" — PULSE loop manifest standard"}]}],"id":"blk-73441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104738","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"spn-104739","text":" — empirical evaluation of topology-aware continual learning"}]}],"id":"blk-73443","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73445","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104740","text":"Documentation index"}]},{"id":"blk-73446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104741","text":"Linked index of every page in this set (renders on GitHub and in the docs atlas; the toctrees above drive the Sphinx build):"}]},{"id":"blk-73447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104742","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guides"}]},{"id":"blk-73448","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104743","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"Quickstart"}]}],"id":"blk-73449","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104744","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/runtime-walkthrough.md"}],"text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]}],"id":"blk-73451","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104745","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/positioning.md"}],"text":"Positioning — The Missing Constraint: Runtime Governance in the Agent Stack"}]}],"id":"blk-73453","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73456","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104746","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/competitive-landscape.md"}],"text":"Competitive Landscape — Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-73455","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104747","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/comparison-table.md"}],"text":"Comparison — OpenSentience vs. Alternatives"}]}],"id":"blk-73457","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73460","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104748","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ecosystem-overview.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem Overview — How the Protocols Connect"}]}],"id":"blk-73459","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104749","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/research.md"}],"text":"Research Overview"}]}],"id":"blk-73461","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104750","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/faq.md"}],"text":"FAQ"}]}],"id":"blk-73463","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104751","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/skills/SKILLS.md"}],"text":"Agent Skills"}]}],"id":"blk-73465","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104752","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-73468","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73470","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104753","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — Embodiment Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-73469","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104754","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-73471","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104755","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-73474","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104756","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-73475","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-73478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104757","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-73477","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-73479","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104758","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-73480","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104759","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-73481","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-73482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104760","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-73483","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104761","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-73484","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104762","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-73485","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-73487","spans":[{"id":"spn-104763","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-73488","spans":[{"id":"spn-104764","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-73489","spans":[{"id":"spn-104765","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-73486","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-73490","spans":[{"id":"spn-104766","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-73491","spans":[{"id":"spn-104767","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-73492","spans":[{"id":"spn-104768","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-73493","spans":[{"id":"spn-104769","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-73494","spans":[{"id":"spn-104770","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-73495","spans":[{"id":"spn-104771","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-104772","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-73496","spans":[{"id":"spn-104773","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-73497","spans":[{"id":"spn-104774","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-73498","spans":[{"id":"spn-104775","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-73499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104776","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-104777","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-104778","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-104779","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-104780","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-104781","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-104782","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-104783","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-104784","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-104785","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-104786","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-104787","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-104788","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-73500","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104789","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-73501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104790","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-104791","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-104792","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-73502","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-73503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104793","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-104794","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-104795","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-73504","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-104796","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-73505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104797","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-104798","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-104799","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-104800","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-104801","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-73506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-104802","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera4ltz6r4wpz4yeqc2wsknaybm4f7a7ogykxxbwjkt6seembyqmqna","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}